# SpecDD kitchen sink fixture for the sample invoice project.
# Whole-line comments are allowed; inline trailing comments are intentionally absent.

Spec: SpecDD Kitchen Sink Fixture

Platform: SpecDD/1.2

Purpose:
  Exercise every documented SpecDD section and common syntax form in one valid fixture.
  Provide a compact reference file for readers, examples, syntax highlighting, validation, and navigation smoke tests.
  Keep the kitchen sink connected to plausible Python fixture files rather than isolated placeholder paths.

Structure:
  ./kitchen-sink.sdd: Complete language coverage fixture.
  ./app.sdd: Fixture project contract.
  ./src/invoice_demo: Python package used by this fixture.
  ./src/invoice_demo/*.py: Python source files with resolvable path references.
  ./src/invoice_demo/*.sdd: Source-adjacent SpecDD files.
  ./tests/*.py: Fixture tests.
  ./tests/*.sdd: Test-adjacent SpecDD files.

Owns:
  ./kitchen-sink.sdd
  ./app.sdd
  ./src/invoice_demo/*
  ./tests/*
  @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService
  Kitchen sink fixture authorship and maintenance

Can modify:
  ./kitchen-sink.sdd
  ./src/invoice_demo/*
  ./tests/*

Can read:
  ./app.sdd
  ./src/invoice_demo/module.sdd
  ./src/invoice_demo/models.py
  ./src/invoice_demo/repository.py
  ./src/invoice_demo/service.py
  ./src/invoice_demo/service.sdd
  ./tests/test_service.py
  ./tests/test_service.sdd

References:
  ./app.sdd
  ./src/invoice_demo/models.py
  ./src/invoice_demo/repository.py
  ./src/invoice_demo/service.py
  ./tests/test_service.py

Must:
  Include every currently documented SpecDD section label.
  Include at least one whole-line comment.
  Include explicit path examples, glob examples, `@` symbol examples, inline code examples, and free-form prose examples.
  Include all documented task states.
  Keep references pointed at files that exist in this fixture tree.
  Remain readable as a single source-adjacent development contract.

Must not:
  Require implementation files outside the fixture tree to change.
  Use inline trailing comments.
  Treat examples as permission to ignore local fixture constraints.
  Expand write authority beyond the paths listed in Can modify.

Forbids:
  ./generated/**
  ./dist/**
  network access
  destructive filesystem commands
  undocumented task state markers

Depends on:
  ./app.sdd
  ./src/invoice_demo/module.sdd
  @invoice_demo.models.Invoice
  @invoice_demo.repository.InvoiceRepository
  @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService

Exposes:
  ./kitchen-sink.sdd
  ./app.sdd
  @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService.create_invoice
  @invoice_demo.cli.create_demo_invoice

Accepts:
  SpecDD version 1.2 section vocabulary
  fixture-root paths
  spec-relative paths
  glob paths such as `./src/invoice_demo/*.py`
  inline code spans such as `InvoiceService.create_invoice`
  task status markers
  Gherkin-like scenario steps
  small concrete examples

Returns:
  a complete kitchen sink .sdd fixture
  a human-readable coverage contract
  parser and highlighter smoke-test input
  navigation examples for fixture source files

Raises:
  MissingSectionCoverageError
  MissingTaskStateCoverageError
  InvalidInlineCommentError
  MissingReferenceError

Handles:
  fixture-root path references
  sibling and parent path references
  inline code spans
  explicit `@` symbol references
  task state coverage
  Given steps
  When steps
  Then steps
  And steps
  But steps

Tasks:
  [x] #0 Include identity sections.
  [x] #1 Include scope and ownership sections.
  [x] #2 Include positive and negative constraint sections.
  [x] #3 Include interface and contract sections.
  [x] #4 Include workflow and behavior sections.
  [ ] #5 Use this fixture in future parser, documentation, or navigation checks.
  [!] #6 Add automated fixture validation when official validation tooling exists.
  [?] #7 Decide whether fixtures should include intentionally invalid examples in a separate file.
  [-] #8 Skip package metadata because this fixture intentionally avoids packaging concerns.
  # This indented comment is still a comment and is not a task.

Done when:
  Every documented section label appears at least once.
  Every documented task state appears at least once.
  Scenarios include Given, When, Then, And, and But steps.
  References resolve to existing fixture or project files.
  The fixture project contains plausible Python code and adjacent specs.

Scenario: every documented section is represented
  Given this kitchen sink fixture is read from top to bottom
  When a reader checks the section labels
  Then Spec, Platform, Purpose, Structure, Owns, Can modify, Can read, References, Must, Must not, Forbids, Depends on, Exposes, Accepts, Returns, Raises, Handles, Tasks, Done when, Scenario, and Example are present
  But no inline trailing comment is required to understand the fixture

Scenario: task states are covered
  Given the allowed task states are open, done, skipped, blocked, and needs decision
  And optional numeric task IDs may be present
  When the Tasks section is scanned
  Then [ ], [x], [-], [!], and [?] are all represented
  And task IDs such as #0 and #8 are visible

Scenario: write authority remains local
  Given this fixture owns ./kitchen-sink.sdd and ./src/invoice_demo/*
  When an agent works under this spec
  Then only fixture paths listed in Can modify may be modified
  And ./app.sdd and ./src/invoice_demo/service.sdd may be read as context
  But ./generated/** and ./dist/** remain forbidden modification targets

Scenario: explicit references are represented
  Given ./src/invoice_demo/service.py creates invoices
  And ./tests/test_service.py checks service behavior
  When @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService.create_invoice is referenced
  Then the symbol uses the explicit at-prefix form
  And `./src/invoice_demo/*.py` remains inline code text with an explicit path inside it

Example:
  input spec path: ./kitchen-sink.sdd
  reference path: ./src/invoice_demo/service.sdd
  glob path: ./src/invoice_demo/*.py
  public symbol: @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService.create_invoice
  accepted task states: [ ] [x] [-] [!] [?]
  accepted scenario words: Given When Then And But
  output file: ./tests/test_service.py
  output status: complete
